It is Sunday evening and quiet in my flat.
Bruno is sleeping on the rug.
Suddenly there is a knock at the door.
Bruno wakes up.
I open the door.
Sabine is standing in the hallway.
Bruno hears her voice.
He runs to her excitedly and greets her.
"Hello, my little dog!" Sabine calls and pets him.
"How was your weekend?" she asks me.
"We had a wonderful weekend," I answer.
"Bruno was really good."
"Thank you very much for your help, Maya," Sabine says.
"You're very welcome," I say and give her the bag.
"Here, you have to take his things back with you."
Sabine thanks me and picks the little dog up.
"Come, Bruno, we are going home," she says.
She takes him in her arms and leaves.
"Bye, you two!" I call out.
Now it is completely quiet here again.
